5_Project_History/history.md:23:- **The orphan-population fixture timeout** (Kamil's find: `psql timed out after 30.0s` at 93,872 documents / 61,095 `anchor_store` rows). His dual-`NOT EXISTS` rewrite is `NOT (A OR B)` ≡ `NOT A AND NOT B` — equivalence-preserving by inspection, so it cannot change the result set, only the plan. Adopted, but landed by Peter rather than accepted as a platform PR: `tests/support/anchoring/anchor_sql.py` is systemTest. Three call sites share the shape. Proof must assert **identical counts**, not just the speed.
Blockchain/Dev/BACKLOG.md:124:- ✅ **Verify endpoint reads document.data.blockchain stub instead of anchor_store row** — Two-part fix in `services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts`: (1) forward the caller's bearer token to anchoring's `/api/anchors/verify/:hash` (anchoring's global authenticate middleware was rejecting unauthed calls with 500 "No token provided", silently failing the live-chain query), (2) parse anchoring's flat response shape `{verified, txHash, blockNumber, confirmedAt, anchoredAt}` instead of expecting a nested `j.anchor.*`. Verified end-to-end: `POST /api/documents/:id/verify` now returns `verified: true, blockchainAnchored: true, source: cardano-live` with the real on-chain txHash and blockHeight.
Blockchain/Dev/BACKLOG.md:129:- ✅ **anchor_store.simulated=false for mock-provider rows** — Same root cause as above. With real provider, simulated=false is correct.
Blockchain/Dev/deployment/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md:111:  UPDATE anchor_store SET simulated = true, updated_at = now()
Blockchain/Dev/deployment/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md:119:  that queries `anchor_store` directly, so reconcile it anyway. Whether to re-anchor the
Blockchain/Dev/deployment/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md:135:  irreplaceable asset is the **anchor index** — `anchor_store`/`anchor_batches`
