Blockchain/Dev/BACKLOG.md:124:- ✅ **Verify endpoint reads document.data.blockchain stub instead of anchor_store row** — Two-part fix in `services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts`: (1) forward the caller's bearer token to anchoring's `/api/anchors/verify/:hash` (anchoring's global authenticate middleware was rejecting unauthed calls with 500 "No token provided", silently failing the live-chain query), (2) parse anchoring's flat response shape `{verified, txHash, blockNumber, confirmedAt, anchoredAt}` instead of expecting a nested `j.anchor.*`. Verified end-to-end: `POST /api/documents/:id/verify` now returns `verified: true, blockchainAnchored: true, source: cardano-live` with the real on-chain txHash and blockHeight.
Blockchain/Dev/CHANGELOG.md:124:- **Verify endpoint surfaces shielded status.** `POST /api/verification/verify` and `/verify-file` responses now include `shielded: boolean` and an optional `midnight: {...}` block drawn from on-chain metadata.
Blockchain/Dev/CHANGELOG.md:204:- `POST /api/verification/verify` (originate) is now chain-first: queries the anchoring verify endpoint before falling back to the tenant DB or platform registry. Resolves the cross-environment verification bug — dev-issued certs can be verified from any other environment or connector because the chain is the shared truth.
Blockchain/Dev/CLI-AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS.md:38:- ❌ **PRIORITY 3 CONFIRMED**: `POST /api/verification/verify` always returns `verified: false` on both envs. DEV returns 400 "Insufficient data for verification. Provide a hash to compare against." even when documentId+contentHash are both supplied. DEMO returns 200 but `verified: false`.
Blockchain/Dev/CLI-AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS.md:148:`POST /api/verification/verify` returns `{"verified": false}` on all environments. This is a critical feature — users must be able to verify documents.
