Blockchain/Testing/USER SIMULATED TEST/runs/2026-04-28_handoff.md:52:| H11 verify reason granularity | ✅ verified | Response now has `checks:{ exists, hashValid, notRevoked, hasSignatures, blockchainAnchored }`. *Nit:* human reason still says "could not be completed at this time" instead of "no signatures yet". |
Blockchain/Testing/USER SIMULATED TEST/runs/2026-04-28_summary.md:47:| **H11** — verify reason text distinguishes "registered but not certified" from "not registered" | ✅ **Verified** (different wording than the brief described, but functionally correct) | Response now includes `checks:{ exists:true, hashValid:true, notRevoked:true, hasSignatures:false, blockchainAnchored:true }` AND the reason explicitly references the doc id and status. Wording: `"Document found (id ..., status: anchored) but verification could not be completed at this time"`. The `checks` object is the real distinguishing signal. *Nit:* the human-readable reason is still vague ("could not be completed at this time") — say "no signatures" instead. |
